15	/// `_deleteRecordingFile` is fire-and-forget (`unawaited`) by design — a
16	/// single microtask tick (`Future<void>.delayed(Duration.zero)`) isn't a
17	/// reliable enough wait for a real `dart:io` file-delete to land under
18	/// full-suite load, so every assertion on the resulting file polls
19	/// instead, bounded to avoid hanging if the delete genuinely never
20	/// happens.
21	Future<void> _waitUntilDeleted(File file) async {
22	  for (var i = 0; i < 50 && file.existsSync(); i++) {
23	    await Future<void>.delayed(const Duration(milliseconds: 10));
24	  }
25	}
